# Use Twist Messages for Robot Motion

## Context and Problem Statement
The TurtleBot3 robot must move according to gestures. We need a control method that integrates with ROS2 and Gazebo.

## Decision Drivers
* TurtleBot3 listens to `/cmd_vel`
* Standard message type required
* Works in simulation and on real hardware

## Considered Options
* geometry_msgs/Twist
* Custom motion message
* Direct Gazebo force application

## Decision Outcome
Chosen option: **Twist messages**, because they are the standard way to control ROS-based differential drive robots.

### Consequences
* Good: Works instantly with TurtleBot3  
* Good: Compatible with real hardware  
* Bad: Velocity-only control (no path planning)  

## Pros and Cons

### Twist
* Good: Native support  
* Good: Zero additional configuration  

### Custom Message
* Good: More flexibility  
* Bad: Requires custom controllers  

### Gazebo Force Application
* Good: Physics-level control  
* Bad: Not portable to real robot  
